implement executable awareness for the python program

From: Skye Soss <skye@soss.website>

Check the script file passed on the command line, the PYTHONSTARTUP file
and a .pyc file reopened by PyRun_SimpleFile() against
SECBIT_EXEC_RESTRICT_FILE. The new REPL reads PYTHONSTARTUP itself, so
make it read the file with io.open_code().

Check stdin with execveat() before running code from it, either as a
script or as the REPL (including -i and PYTHONINSPECT). If the check
fails, consult SECBIT_EXEC_DENY_INTERACTIVE.

The -c and -m options consult SECBIT_EXEC_DENY_INTERACTIVE directly: a
module run with -m can take code from its arguments or stdin. A
directory or zip file passed as the script still runs its __main__
module, which is checked like any other file.

